From 444728e5e9861f503822882f566be205a682ac8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 12:49:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] usb: gadget: dwc2_udc_otg: treat -ENOENT as no clocks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dwc2_udc_otg_clk_init() already treats -ENOSYS ("no clk support") as a
successful no-op, but returns every other error — including -ENOENT,
which clk_get_bulk() returns when the node has no "clocks" property at
all. On CV1800 boards our -u-boot.dtsi overlay deliberately omits a
clocks phandle because U-Boot has no CV1800 USB clock driver, so probe
fails with -ENOENT before reset_init/phy_setup get a chance to run.

The FSBL leaves the USB block clocked and its phy powered; treat
-ENOENT the same as -ENOSYS so the probe succeeds without clocks on
platforms that need it.

Signed-off-by: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/dwc2_udc_otg.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/dwc2_udc_otg.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/dwc2_udc_otg.c
index e475b14b..893297cd 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/dwc2_udc_otg.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/dwc2_udc_otg.c
@@ -1056,7 +1056,7 @@ static int dwc2_udc_otg_clk_init(struct udevice *dev,
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = clk_get_bulk(dev, clks);
-	if (ret == -ENOSYS)
+	if (ret == -ENOSYS || ret == -ENOENT)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (ret)
